Title:
Hollow — Shellcode Loader Generator (Windows PE) with Multiple Injection Templates

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
Hollow is a generator that takes raw shellcode plus a JSON “profile” and produces a compiled Windows PE (EXE or DLL) loader with the payload AES-256-CBC encrypted and embedded. It automates a pipeline of encrypting the shellcode, substituting it into C template placeholders, and compiling a stripped, statically linked binary via MinGW. At runtime, the loader decrypts using Windows BCrypt and executes via the injection technique implemented by the selected template. Included templates cover classic remote thread injection, Early Bird APC injection, and DLL sideloading, with variants that use direct syscalls (Hell’s Gate) to bypass Win32 API-layer telemetry. The repo also documents why Defender behavioral rules often trigger on the VirtualAllocEx/WriteProcessMemory/CreateRemoteThread sequence and how syscall-based templates avoid that specific detection path. It’s primarily useful for red teams/pentesters building customizable loaders and for defenders/researchers studying common injection tradecraft and detection gaps.

Technical Focus:
- Shellcode encryption/embedding (AES-256-CBC) and runtime decryption via BCrypt
- Windows process injection: CreateRemoteThread, VirtualAllocEx, WriteProcessMemory, VirtualProtectEx
- Early Bird APC injection (QueueUserAPC + suspended process)
- Direct syscalls / Hell’s Gate SSN resolution from ntdll stubs
- DLL sideloading and in-process shellcode execution from DLL entry
- Template/profile-driven loader generation and cross-compilation with MinGW

Use Cases:
- Generate engagement-specific Windows EXE/DLL loaders from raw shellcode
- Swap injection techniques quickly via profiles (new process, existing process, APC, sideload)
- Test EDR/Defender behavioral detections against Win32 vs direct-syscall injection paths
- Create and iterate on custom injection templates for operator tradecraft
- Produce source-only substituted templates for manual modification before compilation

Keywords:
shellcode loader, AES-256-CBC, Windows PE, process injection, CreateRemoteThread, VirtualAllocEx, WriteProcessMemory, VirtualProtectEx, Early Bird APC, QueueUserAPC, ResumeThread, direct syscalls, Hell’s Gate, SSN, ntdll, BCrypt, DLL sideloading, MinGW-w64, static linking, Windows Defender behavioral detection